I did it! I finally did it! I ascended for the first time.
I played a lawful Valkyrie. I took the easy way, but hey, first time!

Ok, the beginning was quite devoid of events of remark, bashing
monsters and all that. I #dipped the longsword for Excalibur. I
skipped the Mines and headed for Sokoban first. By level 6 I found
some bones from an old attempt of a barbarian. There weren't many
useful things... at least out of the quite likely cursed bag of
holding I couldn't lift at all. I didn't have a wand of cancellation
handy, so I left the bag around and took a mental note about it. There
were Cleaver and Ogresmasher in those bones. And I thought, "Great,
two artifacts I'll never use. Well, maybe Ogresmasher in the Quest,
for extra style points..."
There was also an altar on that level. I converted it, blessed some
water, started a stash under a boulder, and made a few sacrifices to
increase luck before Sokoban. I knew I would need to "cheat" Sokoban.
There's always some unexpected factor the RNG throws in that forces me
to "cheat". I eventually solved it, after losing some luck because of
some peacefuls (curse you, RNG!). The prize was an amulet of
reflection. It was good, since there was a BoH back there.

I went back to the Mines, hacked a few gnomes, and by the second
level... more bones! This was an unfortunate wizard killed by a
kitten, while vomiting. Mostly starting equipment: a pair of rings, a
few spellbooks, and the cloak of magic resistance every wizard begins
the game with. I put it on, it being cursed or not. It was. One dose
of holy water and everything's fine. Among the bones, Magicbane. Yeah,
I thought, it's good, but I don't want to walk around with it in my
hands... I already had Excalibur and Mjollnir (sometimes I just can't
stop sacrificing...). Plus Cleaver, and Ogresmasher...

And then... Minetown bones! A lawful temple. Apparently the poor guy
was killed after being stripped bare by a pair of nymphs and a
leprechaun. Not much on his grave, but I got his stuff from the nymph
and the leprechaun.
But this time I had already had a decent set of armor (+2 dwarvish
mithril coat, +3 orcish helm, +2 fireproof boots of speed, +2
gauntlets of power), mostly from Cohen, the barbarian, petrified by a
cockatrice corpse, along with reflection and magic resistance. So, his
stuff wasn't very interesting. There was Giantslayer too. So far, I
had already seen six artifacts... No way I would be allowed to wish
for Grayswandir...

After the Mines I was XL 13, so I thought, let's head down and do the
Quest. A blessed potion of gain level puts me at XL 14, and I find the
Quest portal at the rogue level. The Valkyrie quest is so easy...

Ok, so I already had the Bell of Opening and the Orb of Fate. I had
teleport control from a tengu corpse, so now I could go back to my
stash whenever I please.

It was time to rob Fort Ludios. I read a few scrolls of gold
detection, quaff some potions of object detection, and rob all the
vaults, until I find the portal. I put on my ring of conflict and let
the soldiers slaughter each other. I kill Croesus, loot the vault. It
had been a very long time since I had last been in Fort Ludios, and I
was "surprised" by the land mines that are spread all over the vault.

Up next was Medusa. Easy one, since I already had boots of water
walking.

By this time, I still hadn't found a single scroll of identify.
Everything I had identified so far was through prices or
experimentation. I was getting frustrated by this. And no wand of
death in Fort Ludios, at least with any charges left. I started to
regret having used conflict to get rid of the soldiers. But it was
fun.

On the way to Medusa, I finally found a wand of cancellation. Back up,
and loot the BoH I left behind. Guess what, another artifact.
Trollsbane was inside. Holy water, rings, scrolls... but, after
appraisal from a Minetown shopkeeper... No identify. The RNG was
driving me mad! What cruel god would denies his followers the truth?

Back to Medusa, easy, as always, down to the Castle. I take my wooden
flute out of the BoH and play the passtune Tyr had shared with me. I
enter the Castle, kill everything on sight that isn't peaceful, get
the /oW, and wish for... I was tempted to go for ?oI, but I decided to
save the wishes. I scribble a few scrolls of enchant armor with one of
the magic markers I had stored (there were three), raise my AC to -34
and fooproof it. I had something like 250 hp. All seemed ok for
Gehennom. Oh, and I had produced a SDSM from scales in the Castle,
leaving my neck free for some uncursed triangular amulet. Life saving
I hoped, but it turned out to be ESP.

My AK was almost complete. The only missing things were the papyrus
spellbook and the Candelabrum now. I had TONS of C-rations and K-
rations in my stash (yeah, something like 150 K, and 90 C). Izchak
gladly sold me 7 candles. I had so much holy water I could drown
myself on it (70-80 bottles). Wands of digging... Well, let's say with
all those wands I could probably make the Everest look like a small
mound... What I needed was identify, to sort out all the jewelry and
literature I had. It was when I snapped. I decided to identify the
scrolls through reading. There were about 30 or 40 unidentified
scrolls in my stash. So, I grab one worth 100 zm. I think, what can go
wrong with 100-zorkmid scrolls? Fire! Ok, I drop all scrolls, as to
not set them on fire. And I read the scroll. Well, the thing is, I
will never again forget that scrolls of destroy armor are also worth
100 zm. My cloak of magic resistance was gone. I wasn't going to enter
Gehennom without magic resistance! Well, I had a /oW: I wished for a
replacement cloak and entered Gehennom.

Of all the "big" baddies in Gehennom, Juiblex was the only one posing
a threat. He engulfed me. I quickly dispose of him from the inside and
levelport back to the stash with the Orb. I pray and Tyr heals my
illness. By this time I had been crowned some time along the way (I
can't actually remember when), but I had spent more than 5000 turns
without prayer, and I never prayed again after that.

Everything goes well, until... well, it was late and I was getting
sleepy. A typo leads to...
I READ ANOTHER SCROLL OF DESTROY ARMOR AND... curse you RNG! Why the
cloak again?

#invoke the Orb, back to the stash, and... change my wardrobe. Take
off the "oESP, put reflection back on, wish for GDSM, and put on my
old cloak of displacement. "I can live without displacement", I said
to the RNG.

I go and kill the poor Vlad. He's so weak... I finally get to #name a
"oLS. I had found my first polymorph trap in his tower. I levelport
back to the stash, and find out none of the amulets I stashed are
"oLS... Well, I take a = of polymorph control and go back to the
Impaler's tower. I take of the GDSM and step into the trap.
Well, I lay a few cockatrice eggs, and "kill" myself back into human
form through elementary physics. I store the eggs in the sack, put my
GDSM back on and go find the Vibrating Square.

That being done, I go after Rodney. I had just recharged Orcus' wand,
and guess who was the first victim...
At this time, I grow a little careless (again!) and the RNG takes the
opportunity to eat some of my brain off. But, by some twisted sense of
humor, I found a scroll of identify among the remains of that
flayer... The RNG is cruel but knows when to give back... I go back to
the stash and identify most everything with that one scroll and others
I wrote.

I go back, grab the Book of the Dead, /oDig down to the VS, perform
the "bell, book and candle job", kill the high priest, shut up Rodney
with a stoning grenade, and grab the Amulet. Now, it's up all the way!
Oh, I still have to stop by my stash to grab some food, the jewelry,
some bottled blessings, all the gems, the useless artifacts, the
bulldozing equipment...

I enter the Plane of Earth, and again, egg to Rodney's face. "I don't
need your stupid +oDig!"
And then I realized what I had forgotten to bring along. I could dig,
but where to? I forgot a means to find the portals! I had to resort to
the Orb of Fate... It was ok. With the five charges, I found the
portals on Earth, Air and Fire. No fighting at all there. I simply
teleported myself from the entrances to the portals. But the Orb
failed twice, so I was out of charges, in the Plane of Water. Ok, I
shall find this one the hard way. And so I did. Before I entered the
Astral Plane I went through my stuff again to make sure I knew what I
could count on and what I couldn't. I dropped a sagan of wands of
digging, and entered the portal.

Ok, let's find my altar now. Left first. Pestilence. Pestilence! I
forgot about illness! I only had three potions of full healing! And
those went away fast. And the altar was neutral. Back I come and
Pestilence revives. I had a really hard time moving around because I
had to kill lots of ants and the like. And Pestilence caught up with
me. I had to resort to... amulet of life saving. I gave up reflection
for a while, but I would not die. Ok, the amulet turns to dust, I put
reflection back on and head to the center. Death. Death ripped a lot
of hp. I managed to get by. But the altar was chaotic. And all those
'a's slowing me down were making me insane!

So, right it was. And Famine. "I can deal with Famine. I brought
fifteen K-rations with me. That should be enough." And then I came to
my senses and... Why eat when I can have slow digestion? Away with
sustain ability. I get past Famine, reach the altar and #offer N - the
Amulet of Yendor named the Real One.

That was it. It took me seven years.


